  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "If a number \\(N,\\) \\(N\\ne0,\\) diminished by four times its reciprocal, equals a given real constant \\(R,\\) then, for this given \\(R,\\) the sum of all such possible values of \\(N\\) is:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac1R\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(R\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(4\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac14\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(-R\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "b",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1969-p5.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Multiplying \\(N-\\frac{4}{N}=R\\) by \\(N\\) gives \\[ N^2-RN-4=0. \\] The sum of its two roots is \\(R\\) by Vieta’s formulas. Both roots are nonzero because their product is \\(-4.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Rewrite \\(N-\\frac{4}{N}=R\\) as a quadratic in \\(N\\)",
        "Use the sum of the roots of that quadratic"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
